COMP2404 Assignment 1 - Bank Transaction Manager

Author
Jackson Lafrance

Purpose
This program manages customers, accounts, and transactions for a bank.

Source Files
Account.cc      Implements the Account class
Bank.cc         Implements the Bank class
Customer.cc     Implements the Customer class
Date.cc         Implements the Date class
Transaction.cc  Implements the Transaction class
main.cc         Implements the main control flow and the provided global stuff

Header Files
Account.h      Declares the Account class
Bank.h         Declares the Bank class
Customer.h     Declares the Customer class
Date.h         Declares the Date class
Transaction.h  Declares the Transaction class
defs.h         Declares all the constants stuff

Other Files
Makefile compiles and links the program and provides the clean and also Readme is this one

Data Files
None

Compilation
In the directory containing the program files, run:

    make

This separately compiles each source file and links the resulting object files
to create an executable named a1. The program requires a C++11-compatible g++
compiler and no external libraries.

Launching
Run the program with:

    ./a1 or make run

Cleaning
To remove the .o files, run:

    make clean
